{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1926, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nThis problem is a simplified version of Problem F.\n\nYou are given an integer sequence of length N: A = (A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N).\nWhen splitting A at one position into two non-empty (contiguous) subarrays, find the maximum possible sum of the counts of distinct integers in those subarrays.\nMore formally, find the maximum sum of the following two values for an integer i such that 1 \\leq i \\leq N-1: the count of distinct integers in (A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i), and the count of distinct integers in (A_{i+1}, A_{i+2}, \\ldots, A_N).\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 A_2 \\ldots A_N\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 2 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\times 10^5\n- 1 \\leq A_i \\leq N (1 \\leq i \\leq N)\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n5\n3 1 4 1 5\n\nSample Output 1\n\n5\n\n\n- For i=1, (3) contains 1 distinct integer, and (1,4,1,5) contains 3 distinct integers, for a total of 4.\n- For i=2, (3,1) contains 2 distinct integers, and (4,1,5) contains 3 distinct integers, for a total of 5.\n- For i=3, (3,1,4) contains 3 distinct integers, and (1,5) contains 2 distinct integers, for a total of 5.\n- For i=4, (3,1,4,1) contains 3 distinct integers, and (5) contains 1 distinct integer, for a total of 4.\n\nTherefore, the maximum sum is 5 for i=2,3.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n10\n2 5 6 5 2 1 7 9 7 2\n\nSample Output 2\n\n8\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1966, "char_start": 1938, "quote": "Input:\n5\n3 1 4 1 5\nOutput:\n5", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 2017, "char_start": 1978, "quote": "Input:\n10\n2 5 6 5 2 1 7 9 7 2\nOutput:\n8", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "c1ce555c68e9d3882e8e3df36ea08a4980449ad601ba2dda6d0f13b0c6ca4930", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "254ae95b2729d55d4201acf2e3ca75c5546106f4ce7c2c741938b5984ec20c82", "seq": 2}
